  "description": "Rustic explicitly uses Rabin with a 1 MiB average, 512 KiB minimum and 8 MiB maximum, Zstd 3, and 8 MiB data/tree pack targets with growth disabled. Gutch uses a nominal 1 MiB FastCDC target, Zstd 3 and 8 MiB compressed bundles. Chunk boundaries, compression units and hashes differ; Rustic remains encrypted. Recovery verifies existing bytes and deletes extra files. Fresh repositories and isolated caches. Four workers where exposed; native Borg/BPT scheduling. One warm-up and 1 rotating measured repetitions; profiling off. Measurement contract 2 separates content repair, preserved-mtime damage, extra-file cleanup and full restoration. Strict source-derived SHA-256 validation follows every supported operation; both native and validation-inclusive durations are reported. Unsupported operations receive no timing.",
